            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ComfortCook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The dried beef is salty and I always rinse the beef under cold tap water and dry between paper towels. I do this for any recipe that calls for dried beef. There's really no other way around the salt, and it doesn't affect the real beef taste for the recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brenda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Rinse the dried beef under cold water, omit the onion juice and use lemon juice instead, add 1/4 cup Cracker Barrel Sharp Cheese (You have to use the Cracker Barrel Sharp Cheese) I have tried other sharp cheeses and there is just something about the taste of Cracker Barrel that make this cheeseball.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-23T15:08:49.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SpeedyCake7597"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making this for year and love it! I use Budig brand beef lunch meat it's not as salty! No need to add the onion juice. If you make it ahead and refrigerate it has plenty of onion flavor. I don't use green pepper but I use green onion for color!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-16T13:32:29.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cindy Lou Shultz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make a version of this every year, but never thought of adding green peppers. I used other suggestions and cut back on worchestershire sauce and used liguid smoke instead of onion juice. Also added a little garlic powder. I meant to roll it in bacon pieces but forgot to. I put a few drops of orange food coloring in it for a Halloween Party and shaped it like a pumpkin. It was excellent. I will use this from now on.",
            "datePublished": "2007-10-31T09:17:09.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dawn Meyer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just use the dried beef green onions and cream cheese. And have had at times put shredded cheese in it to.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-22T08:29:52.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
